## 3. Design System Architecture

### The CSS Custom Property Foundation

The entire design system lives in `index.css` using HSL-based CSS custom properties. This is the **single source of truth** for every color in the app:

```css
:root {
  /* Semantic tokens — used everywhere via Tailwind */
  --background: 0 0% 100%;
  --foreground: 215 35% 15%;
  --card: 0 0% 100%;
  --primary: 215 35% 15%;        /* Deep navy */
  --accent: 0 75% 45%;           /* Rich crimson red */
  --muted: 210 20% 96%;
  --border: 214 32% 91%;
  --ring: 0 75% 45%;
  --radius: 0.75rem;

  /* Brand-specific extensions */
  --vs-navy: 215 35% 15%;
  --vs-red: 0 75% 45%;
  --vs-teal: 171 45% 25%;
  --vs-sand: 33 30% 96%;

  /* Custom easing curves */
  --ease-out: cubic-bezier(0.23, 1, 0.32, 1);
  --ease-in-out: cubic-bezier(0.77, 0, 0.175, 1);
  --ease-drawer: cubic-bezier(0.32, 0.72, 0, 1);
}

.dark {
  --background: 224 71% 4%;
  --foreground: 210 40% 98%;
  --card: 224 71% 4%;
  --accent: 0 75% 45%;           /* Accent stays consistent */
  --muted: 217.2 32.6% 17.5%;
  --border: 217.2 32.6% 17.5%;
}
```

### Why HSL Format?
HSL values without the `hsl()` wrapper allow Tailwind to compose opacity modifiers:
```html
<!-- This works because --accent is just "0 75% 45%" -->
<div class="bg-accent/10">  <!-- 10% opacity accent -->
<div class="text-accent">   <!-- Full accent color -->
```

### The Golden Rule
> **Never write a raw color value in a component.** Always reference a semantic token. If `#1a2b3c` appears in your JSX, you've broken the system.

