## 4. Typography Strategy

### Font Pairing
We use a **two-font system** — a display font for headings and a body font for prose:

| Role | Font | Weights | Usage |
|------|------|---------|-------|
| **Display** (`font-display`) | **Outfit** | 600–900 | Headings, CTAs, navigation labels, badges |
| **Body** (`font-body`) | **Inter** | 300–700 | Paragraphs, form inputs, descriptions |

```css
/* Loaded via Google Fonts */
@import url('https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=Outfit:wght@300;400;500;600;700;800;900&family=Inter:wght@300;400;500;600;700&display=swap');

body {
  font-family: 'Inter', sans-serif;
  font-feature-settings: "cv02", "cv03", "cv04", "ss01", "kern";
  letter-spacing: -0.015em;
}

h1, h2, h3, h4, h5, h6 {
  font-family: 'Outfit', sans-serif;
}
```

### Fluid Typography Scale
Instead of fixed sizes, we use `clamp()` for responsive scaling:

```css
h1 { font-size: clamp(3rem, 7vw, 6.5rem); line-height: 0.9; }
h2 { font-size: clamp(2.5rem, 5vw, 5rem); line-height: 0.95; }
h3 { font-size: clamp(2rem, 4vw, 3.5rem); line-height: 1; }
```

### The "Small Text Legibility" Fix
Admin panels use tiny label text (`text-[9px]`, `text-[10px]`). We override these globally to ensure readability:

```css
.text-[10px], .text-xs { font-size: 0.8rem; letter-spacing: 0.05em; }
.text-[9px] { font-size: 0.75rem; letter-spacing: 0.08em; }
```

### Typography Utility Classes
```css
.heading-hero   { @apply text-5xl md:text-8xl font-black tracking-tight leading-[0.85] uppercase; }
.heading-display { @apply text-4xl md:text-7xl font-black tracking-tight leading-none; }
.text-balance    { text-wrap: balance; }
```

