## 5. Color System & Theming

### The VS Palette Philosophy
Victor Springs uses a **corporate luxury** palette:

| Token | Light Mode | Dark Mode | Semantic Role |
|-------|-----------|-----------|---------------|
| `--primary` | Deep Navy `hsl(215, 35%, 15%)` | Same | Authority, structure |
| `--accent` | Crimson Red `hsl(0, 75%, 45%)` | Same | CTAs, interactive highlights |
| `--vs-teal` | Forest Teal `hsl(171, 45%, 25%)` | Brighter teal | Trust, secondary accent |
| `--vs-sand` | Warm Sand `hsl(33, 30%, 96%)` | Near-black | Section backgrounds |
| `--background` | White | Near-black `hsl(224, 71%, 4%)` | Page base |
| `--muted-foreground` | Slate gray | Light gray | Labels, captions |

### Dark Mode Strategy
We use a **class-based dark mode** (`dark` class on `<html>`) rather than `prefers-color-scheme`. This gives users explicit control via a toggle. The `ThemeContext` stores the preference in `localStorage`:

```jsx
// ThemeContext pattern
const { theme, toggleTheme } = useTheme();
// Renders a sun/moon toggle that adds/removes .dark from <html>
```

### Color Application Patterns
```html
<!-- ✅ Correct: semantic tokens -->
<div class="bg-card border-border text-foreground">
<button class="bg-accent text-accent-foreground">

<!-- ❌ Wrong: hardcoded brand colors -->
<div class="bg-[#1a2b3c]">
<button class="bg-red-600">
```

