## 6. Component Architecture Patterns

### The shadcn/ui Foundation
We don't build UI primitives from scratch. Instead, we use **shadcn/ui** — a collection of copy-paste Radix UI components that live in your codebase under `src/components/ui/`:

```
src/components/ui/
├── button.jsx        # Variant-driven button (default, outline, ghost, destructive)
├── card.jsx          # Card, CardHeader, CardContent, CardTitle, CardDescription
├── dialog.jsx        # Modal dialogs with Radix portal
├── input.jsx         # Styled input with ring focus states
├── badge.jsx         # Status badges (approved, pending, etc.)
├── select.jsx        # Accessible dropdown select
├── skeleton.jsx      # Loading placeholder
└── ...
```

### Custom Components We Built

| Component | Purpose | Key Pattern |
|-----------|---------|-------------|
| `AdminPageShell` | Wraps every admin page with consistent header, breadcrumbs | Layout composition |
| `MobileBottomNav` | iOS-style bottom tab bar with scroll-hide behavior | Scroll listener + AnimatePresence |
| `GlobalSearchDialog` | `⌘K` command palette for property search | Keyboard shortcut + Dialog |
| `ImageUploadField` | Drag-and-drop Cloudinary upload | FormData + progress tracking |
| `SEO` | Dynamic `<head>` meta tags per page | React Helmet pattern |
| `AdminPager` | Shared pagination component | Controlled page state |

### The `AdminPageShell` Pattern
Every admin page wraps its content in a consistent shell:

```jsx
<AdminPageShell
  title="Verification Reports"
  description="Monitor audits, vetted owners, and platform statistics."
>
  {/* Page-specific content */}
</AdminPageShell>
```

This eliminates the need to manually add page headers, dark mode classes, and layout padding to every admin route.

