## 7. Animation & Motion Design

### Framer Motion Patterns We Used

#### 1. Staggered List Entrance
```jsx
const containerVariants = {
  hidden: { opacity: 0 },
  visible: {
    opacity: 1,
    transition: { staggerChildren: 0.1 }
  }
};

const itemVariants = {
  hidden: { opacity: 0, y: 20 },
  visible: { opacity: 1, y: 0, transition: { duration: 0.5 } }
};

<motion.div variants={containerVariants} initial="hidden" animate="visible">
  {items.map(item => (
    <motion.div key={item.id} variants={itemVariants}>
      {/* content */}
    </motion.div>
  ))}
</motion.div>
```

#### 2. Scroll-Triggered Animations
```jsx
<motion.div
  variants={cardVariants}
  initial="hidden"
  whileInView="visible"
  viewport={{ once: true, margin: "-100px" }}
>
```

#### 3. Spring-Based Card Hover
```jsx
<motion.div
  whileHover={{ y: -6 }}
  variants={{
    hidden: { opacity: 0, y: 30 },
    visible: {
      opacity: 1, y: 0,
      transition: { type: "spring", stiffness: 300, damping: 24 }
    }
  }}
>
```

#### 4. Infinite Marquee Strip
```jsx
<motion.div
  animate={{ x: [0, -1035] }}
  transition={{ duration: 20, repeat: Infinity, ease: "linear" }}
  className="flex items-center gap-8"
>
  {[...Array(4)].map((_, j) => (
    <div key={j} className="flex items-center gap-8">
      {phrases.map((phrase, i) => (
        <span className="font-display font-bold uppercase tracking-widest text-sm">
          {phrase}
        </span>
      ))}
    </div>
  ))}
</motion.div>
```

#### 5. SVG Path Drawing (Hero Ribbon)
```jsx
<motion.path
  d="M 0,500 C 300,700 700,300 1000,500"
  fill="none"
  stroke="hsl(var(--primary))"
  strokeWidth="2"
  initial={{ pathLength: 0 }}
  animate={{ pathLength: 1 }}
  transition={{ duration: 3, ease: "easeInOut", repeat: Infinity, repeatType: "mirror" }}
/>
```

### Custom Easing Curves
```css
--ease-out: cubic-bezier(0.23, 1, 0.32, 1);       /* Fast start, slow finish */
--ease-in-out: cubic-bezier(0.77, 0, 0.175, 1);    /* Dramatic S-curve */
--ease-drawer: cubic-bezier(0.32, 0.72, 0, 1);     /* iOS sheet feel */
```

### The Rule of Subtlety
> Animations should feel like **natural physics**, not circus tricks. If a user notices the animation *as an animation*, it's too much. The goal is "this feels alive" — not "this is distracting."

