## 10. Admin Dashboard Design Language

### Visual Vocabulary for Admin Pages

| Element | Treatment |
|---------|-----------|
| **Page headers** | Handled by `AdminPageShell` — consistent title + description |
| **Cards** | `rounded-2xl border overflow-hidden shadow-sm` with dark mode variants |
| **Tables** | Full-width with `divide-y divide-black/[0.02]` subtle row separators |
| **Labels** | `text-[10px] font-black uppercase tracking-[0.2em] text-muted-foreground` |
| **Badges** | Rounded pills with semantic colors (green=approved, amber=pending, red=rejected) |
| **Action buttons** | `rounded-xl h-12 text-[10px] uppercase tracking-widest shadow-lg` |
| **Modals** | `rounded-[3rem] border-none shadow-sm p-12 max-w-md bg-card` |
| **Search inputs** | `h-12 rounded-2xl bg-white/50 border-none` with icon prefix |

### The "Operational Cockpit" Aesthetic
Admin panels should feel like a **mission control center** — dense with information but never cluttered. Key techniques:

1. **Ultra-wide tracking on labels**: `tracking-[0.2em]` or `tracking-widest` on uppercase labels
2. **Extreme font weight contrast**: Labels at `font-black` (900), values at `font-bold` (700) or `font-semibold` (600)
3. **Micro-borders**: `border-black/[0.03]` — barely visible structure lines
4. **Generous padding**: `p-8` minimum on cards, `py-6 px-8` on table cells

