## 11. Mobile-First Responsive Strategies

### Scroll-Aware Bottom Navigation
The `MobileBottomNav` hides on scroll-down and shows on scroll-up:

```jsx
React.useEffect(() => {
  const handleScroll = () => {
    const currentScrollY = window.scrollY;
    if (currentScrollY > lastScrollY.current && currentScrollY > 80) {
      setIsVisible(false);  // Scrolling down — hide
    } else {
      setIsVisible(true);   // Scrolling up — show
    }
    lastScrollY.current = currentScrollY;
  };
  window.addEventListener("scroll", handleScroll, { passive: true });
  return () => window.removeEventListener("scroll", handleScroll);
}, []);
```

### Mobile CSS Overrides (index.css)
```css
@media (max-width: 640px) {
  /* Prevent giant headings on small screens */
  h1, h2 { font-size: clamp(2rem, 10vw, 3.5rem) !important; }
  
  /* Normalize padding */
  .px-6, .px-8, .px-10, .px-12 {
    padding-left: 1rem !important;
    padding-right: 1rem !important;
  }
  
  /* Prevent width overflow */
  .w-60, .w-72, .w-96 {
    width: min(100%, calc(100vw - 1.5rem)) !important;
  }
  
  /* Reset card typography so tailwind classes work inside cards */
  [class*="rounded-2xl"] h3,
  [class*="rounded-2xl"] p {
    font-size: inherit !important;
    line-height: inherit !important;
  }
}
```

### Touch-Optimized Marquee
On mobile, the infinite marquee also supports **drag/swipe** interaction:
```css
.marquee-draggable {
  overflow-x: auto;
  -webkit-overflow-scrolling: touch;
  touch-action: pan-x pan-y;
  cursor: grab;
  scrollbar-width: none;
}
```

