## 12. Backend API Design for CMS

### Flask Blueprint Architecture
Each feature gets its own blueprint file:

```
app/api/
├── auth.py              # Login, register, JWT refresh, password reset
├── properties.py        # CRUD for property listings
├── site_content.py      # CMS content blocks
├── content_items.py     # Blog/article CRUD
├── media.py             # Media library upload/management
├── users.py             # User profiles, role management
├── audit.py             # Activity logging
├── admin_reports.py     # Dashboard analytics
├── settings.py          # App-wide configuration
└── ...
```

### Registration in `__init__.py`
```python
from app.api.site_content import site_content_bp
from app.api.content_items import content_items_bp
from app.api.media import media_bp

app.register_blueprint(site_content_bp, url_prefix='/api/site-content')
app.register_blueprint(content_items_bp, url_prefix='/api/content-items')
app.register_blueprint(media_bp, url_prefix='/api/media')
```

### Admin-Only Route Protection
```python
@content_items_bp.route('/', methods=['POST'])
@jwt_required()
def create_content_item():
    user_id = get_jwt_identity()
    user = User.query.get(user_id)
    if not user or user.role != 'admin':
        return jsonify({'message': 'Admin access required'}), 403
    # ... create logic
```

### Pagination Pattern
```python
@content_items_bp.route('/', methods=['GET'])
def list_content_items():
    page = request.args.get('page', 1, type=int)
    per_page = request.args.get('per_page', 12, type=int)
    
    query = ContentItem.query
    
    # Filtering
    content_type = request.args.get('type')
    if content_type:
        query = query.filter_by(type=content_type)
    
    # Search
    search = request.args.get('search')
    if search:
        query = query.filter(
            db.or_(
                ContentItem.title.ilike(f'%{search}%'),
                ContentItem.summary.ilike(f'%{search}%')
            )
        )
    
    # Paginate
    pagination = query.order_by(ContentItem.created_at.desc()).paginate(
        page=page, per_page=per_page, error_out=False
    )
    
    return jsonify({
        'items': [item.to_dict() for item in pagination.items],
        'total': pagination.total,
        'page': page,
        'pages': pagination.pages
    })
```

