## 14. Deployment Pipeline & Build Hygiene

### Vercel Auto-Deploy Flow
```
Developer pushes to main → GitHub webhook → Vercel clones → npm install → vite build → Deploy
```

### Common Build Breakers We Encountered

| Error | Cause | Fix |
|-------|-------|-----|
| `The symbol "X" has already been declared` | Duplicate import statement | Remove the duplicate line |
| `Unexpected closing "X" tag does not match opening "Y" tag` | Mismatched JSX tags after refactor | Audit the JSX tree, ensure every open tag has a matching close |
| `Unexpected end of file before closing tag` | Missing closing tag | Add the missing `</Component>` |
| Corrupted code block | Bad merge/paste during bulk edit | Diff against previous commit, remove duplicated code |

### Pre-Push Build Check (Recommended)
Always run `npm run build` locally before pushing. If npm isn't available locally, at minimum validate JSX structure by eye for:
1. Every `<Component>` has a `</Component>`
2. No duplicate imports
3. No stray code from copy/paste errors

